# Ignored, self-validating caches that wt0 copy-on-write clones from the base
# checkout into every new worktree before anything runs in it, so the first
# Nx/Next build starts warm. Mirrors the "Seeding" policy in
# https://github.com/lonormaly/worktree-zero/blob/main/docs/lifecycle.md
#
# node_modules is deliberately NOT listed here: wt0 0.1.16 seeds it
# automatically behind a byte-identical lockfile, gated on the base's manager
# having no cheaper active native store. This project runs Bun's isolated
# linker with globalStore = true (see bunfig.toml) — an active native
# link-tree store — so that gate refuses the clone by design ("native store
# is cheaper: bun global store") and every worktree links into the shared
# global store instead, which already measures cheaper than a wt0 clone.

.nx/cache

apps/blog/.next/cache
apps/landing/.next/cache
apps/web/.next/cache
